 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Not at all, many restaurants check after you' finished. Asking now gives them service they' shown you have, rather than waiting. You can do that a few ways. You can each pay for your own food and then share the check, or you can split exactly what each ate. The restaurant usually tells you the total each of you should aim for. If you go over by few pounds, nobody gets upset, it's nothing intentional. You' welcome. Just remember, checking the bill right after eating is polite, and splitting it fairly takes into account anyone who overeats.",
